    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** (85.94) and **James Wood** (76.28) headline our production expectations. **Corbin Carroll** is an absolute priority start; the intersection of a favorable matchup against Chandler (5.00 xERA) and the 100% stolen base expectation against his slow delivery makes him our daily ceiling play. Similarly, **James Wood** is locked into a prime spot atop the order against Bieber, where his elite 0.425 xwOBA provides a high floor for Runs and RBI. **Mickey Moniak** (75.94) also ranks among our strongest plays, leveraging a significant +14% dynamic platoon advantage against King, proving that our roster depth is effectively neutralizing mid-tier starters today.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical tightropes, most notably with **Isaac Paredes** (43.49), whose score suffers under the weight of a negative platoon split and a tough matchup against Detmers. He remains in the starting lineup only due to the depth requirements of our format. Conversely, the most difficult bench decision involved **Travis Bazzana** (46.83); he was the final cut from our utility rotation, ultimately losing out to **Vinnie Pasquantino** (62.65), who possesses a more favorable park factor and a substantial +14% platoon edge against Bradley. While we have several players currently listed as \"Lineup Pending,\" including **Dalton Rushing**, **Josh Naylor**, and **Cole Young**, we are confident that their positional hierarchy will hold. We continue to monitor the status of **Jose Caballero** and **Trevor Story**, who remain unavailable due to roster moves and injury, respectively, forcing us to lean heavily on our active bench pieces like **Zach McKinstry** if any late-scratch lineup shifts occur.",
